        81.83369445800781
      ],
      "text": "Contact investigation : Another implementation consideration is the scale up contact investigation",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        80.59070587158203,
        527.4454956054688,
        95.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "approaches, which can improve early case detection of children with non-severe disease who may",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        93.79071807861328,
        234.60440063476562,
        108.23371887207031
      ],
      "text": "benefit from the 4-month regimen.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.47807312011719,
        115.38463592529297,
        524.4636840820312,
        129.93763732910156
      ],
      "text": "Use of ethambutol in the intensive phase of treatment : Children and young adolescents with non-",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 10.95792007446289,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        128.69459533691406,
        527.1990966796875,
        143.13758850097656
      ],
      "text": "severe TB who live in settings with low HIV prevalence or a low prevalence of isoniazid resistance and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.99484920501709,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        141.8946075439453,
        527.4790649414062,
        156.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "those who are HIV negative can be treated with a three-drug regimen (HRZ) for two months, followed",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.973318099975586,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        155.09474182128906,
        527.41455078125,
        169.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "by two months of HR. Children and young adolescents with non-severe TB who are living in settings",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        168.29469299316406,
        527.4142456054688,
        182.73768615722656
      ],
      "text": "where the prevalence of HIV is high  and/or the prevalence of isoniazid resistance is high  should  16 17",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        181.4947052001953,
        527.4442138671875,
        195.9376983642578
      ],
      "text": "be treated with HRZE for two months followed by HR for two months. In the SHINE trial, ethambutol",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        194.69471740722656,
        527.3967895507812,
        209.13771057128906
      ],
      "text": "was used in line with these recommendations as per national guidelines and all CALHIV received",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        207.8946075439453,
        527.3946533203125,
        222.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "ethambutol as part of their treatment. For the six-month regimen used to treat more severe forms",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        221.09474182128906,
        430.15252685546875,
        235.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "of TB, it is recommended to add ethambutol to the regimen (i.e. 4HRZE/2HR).",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.47807312011719,
        242.6885986328125,
        527.4351806640625,
        257.2416076660156
      ],
      "text": "Child-friendly formulations : NTPs are encouraged to prioritize the use of child-friendly fixed dose",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        255.9987335205078,
        527.3806762695312,
        270.4417419433594
      ],
      "text": "combination (FDC) formulations for TB treatment in children up to 25 kg body weight, such as: the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        269.1986083984375,
        527.5572509765625,
        283.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "3-FDC HRZ 50/75/150 mg with or without the addition of dispersible ethambutol, and the 2-FDC HR",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.999149322509766,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        282.39862060546875,
        527.4496459960938,
        296.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "50/75 mg (available from the Stop TB Partnership’s Global Drug Facility (GDF)). Capacity building of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        295.5986328125,
        527.4046630859375,
        310.0416564941406
      ],
      "text": "health care workers at all levels of the health system on diagnostic approaches (including treatment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        308.798583984375,
        527.3075561523438,
        323.2416076660156
      ],
      "text": "decision algorithms), eligibility for the four-month regimen and monitoring of children on first-line TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.994048118591309,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        321.99859619140625,
        498.3306884765625,
        336.4416198730469
      ],
      "text": "treatment will also be critical factors in the successful implementation of the shorter regimen.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.47807312011719,
        343.592529296875,
        527.4166259765625,
        358.1455383300781
      ],
      "text": "Treatment of severe pulmonary TB in children and young adolescents:  Children and young",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        356.9026184082031,
        527.3969116210938,
        371.34564208984375
      ],
      "text": "adolescents with forms of PTB that do not meet the eligibility criteria for the four-month regimen",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        370.10260009765625,
        527.6356811523438,
        384.5456237792969
      ],
      "text": "should be treated with a standard six-month regimen that includes a fourth drug (ethambutol) in the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.998199462890625,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        383.3025207519531,
        243.6321258544922,
        397.74554443359375
      ],
      "text": "intensive phase (such as 2HRZE/4HR).",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.47807312011719,
        404.8965148925781,
        527.5084838867188,
        419.44952392578125
      ],
      "text": "Treatment options for adolescents from 12 years of age : Another implementation consideration",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 10.998199462890625,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        418.2065124511719,
        527.4486694335938,
        432.6495361328125
      ],
      "text": "is that adolescents aged 12 years and above with TB can benefit from the four-month regimen that",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        431.406494140625,
        527.4199829101562,
        445.8495178222656
      ],
      "text": "consists of isoniazid, rifapentine, moxifloxacin and pyrazinamide (HPMZ), which is now conditionally",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        444.60650634765625,
        527.5816650390625,
        459.0495300292969
      ],
      "text": "recommended by WHO (see Recommendation 2.1 in the current document). Adolescents aged",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        457.8065185546875,
        527.5830688476562,
        472.2495422363281
      ],
      "text": "between 12 and 16 years therefore have three options for treatment: the four-month HPMZ regimen,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.98529052734375,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        471.0065002441406,
        527.1148681640625,
        485.44952392578125
      ],
      "text": "the four-month 2HRZ(E)/2HR regimen, and the standard six-month 2HRZ(E)/4HR regimen. Adolescents",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.94486141204834,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        484.2065124511719,
        524.42138671875,
        498.6495361328125
      ],
      "text": "from 16 years of age were not included in the SHINE trial and therefore have two options: the four-",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        497.406494140625,
        404.47528076171875,
        511.8495178222656
      ],
      "text": "month HPMZ regimen and the standard six-month 2HRZE/4HR regimen.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        519.1104125976562,
        527.1738891601562,
        533.5534057617188
      ],
      "text": "Choosing an appropriate regimen for this age group will depend on clinical factors (such as the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        532.3104248046875,
        527.5035400390625,
        546.75341796875
      ],
      "text": "presence of severe disease or if living with HIV, ART status and CD4 count) as well as contextual factors",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.971663475036621,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        545.5103759765625,
        361.5290832519531,
        559.953369140625
      ],
      "text": "(including the availability of the HPMZ regimen in the country).",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        573.3275756835938,
        220.46530151367188,
        589.1796264648438
      ],
      "text": "Monitoring and evaluation",
      "font": "SegoeUI-BoldItalic",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        596.3875732421875,
        527.3927001953125,
        610.83056640625
      ],
      "text": "The clinical monitoring requirements for the shorter regimen remain the same as for the six-month",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        609.5875854492188,
        479.9506530761719,
        624.0305786132812
      ],
      "text": "regimen and treatment outcomes are determined at the end of the four-month regimen.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        631.2916259765625,
        527.416748046875,
        645.734619140625
      ],
      "text": "Should there be insufficient clinical improvement after completion of the four-month regimen, the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        644.4915161132812,
        527.176025390625,
        658.9345092773438
      ],
      "text": "clinician may decide to extend treatment to six months while considering alternative diagnoses,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        657.6915283203125,
        147.44810485839844,
        672.134521484375
      ],
      "text": "including DR-TB.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        718.2373046875,
        526.7864990234375,
        731.9412841796875
      ],
      "text": "This level of resistance was defined as countries, subnational administrative units, or selected facilities, where the HIV prevalence among  16",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 7.993647575378418,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        731.0372924804688,
        526.7337036132812,
        741.541259765625
      ],
      "text": "adult pregnant women is ≥1% or among TB patients is ≥5% in the Guidance for national tuberculosis programmes on the management",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 7.989543437957764,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        740.6373291015625,
        242.93727111816406,
        751.1412963867188
      ],
      "text": "of tuberculosis in children (second edition) 2014.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        749.8719482421875,
        526.5911865234375,
        763.5758666992188
      ],
      "text": "WHO does not intend to establish thresholds for low, moderate or high levels of prevalence of isoniazid resistance; instead NTPs will  17",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        762.6719360351562,
        226.29014587402344,
        773.1759033203125
      ],
      "text": "establish definitions for their own countries.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
